## [ENT-002] | 2026-09-14 06:43 UTC | Neo | error | ref: agentic-brain:reflections/2026-09-14_neo_better-indicators-can-hide-worse-owner-outcomes.md | see: 20260914T062349Z
Failure class: a successful proxy check does not establish the economic claim (R20).
Evidence: raw statement checks coexisted with normalization and ownership issues;
initial output was too large for the requested use. Source review exposed debt
components that could not safely substitute for complete current borrowings.
Root cause: implicit scale, sign, period and claimholder assumptions between stages.
Fix: source-local mappings, regression fixtures, actual Q4 EPS, explicit borrowing
coverage and separate units; compact output with material missingness preserved.
The final financial-data review reported 435 passed tests and one optional skip.
Research counterexamples also distinguish favorable EPS, margins and aggregate
returns from owner value; the research skill now checks the intervening inference.
Qualifications to shared Library claims are documented in Neo's knowledge files,
not silently applied to other authors' work. No investment framework changed here.
Reflection: 20260914T062349Z.

## [ENT-003] | 2026-09-15 10:56 UTC | Neo | error | ref: agentic-brain:reflections/2026-09-15_neo_learning-is-not-a-file-quota.md | see: 20260915T103729Z
Failure class: caller assumptions can contradict the referenced workflow (R8/R20).
Evidence: the research helper presumed most answers were already in the Brain
and implied one new file per cycle, while capture allowed create/update/confirm.
A separate later execution kernel lacked a previously defined helper; that
attempt failed before a workspace write.
Root cause: duplicated completion assumptions and treating live variables as
persistent evidence of recoverable task state.
Fix: the research helper defers to the capture outcome contract; scripted
batches reload task-local code and consult the persisted completed-cycle record.
Verification: fresh-namespace helper loading and completed-cycle replay rejection
passed; researched outcomes retain source and numerical verification separately.
Closure publication initially paused at a tool-approval timeout, not a Git
failure; Suggi explicitly confirmed resumption. No approval bypass was used.
Reflection: 20260915T103729Z.

## [ENT-004] | 2026-09-23 16:25 UTC | Neo | error | ref: agentic-brain:reflections/2026-09-23_neo_bound-research-not-completion.md | see: 20260923T161317Z
Failure class: successful retrieval or a component check can conceal an
unfinished or unsupported report (R20), with caller-scope contradictions (R8).
Evidence: an earlier discovery-heavy run ended without a report; quote fields
conflicted on previous-close baselines; a shorter rerun did not match the
Human's preference for the earlier fuller explanation.
Fix: bounded discovery, comparable dated quote baselines, venue calendars,
and caller-owned report/capture/task boundaries in the profile-local skills.
Static routing checks and personally completed earlier reports are verified;
the new bond-plus-capture report remains an unperformed integration test.
Closure also caught a citation helper allocating a duplicate from sparse
legacy IDs before publication. Separate registration and a collision guard
preserved prior mappings; the underlying helper repair is explicitly open.
No portfolio, protected investment method or scheduler activation changed.
Reflection: 20260923T161317Z.

## [ENT-005] | 2026-09-24 11:14 UTC | Neo | error | ref: agentic-brain:reflections/2026-09-24_neo_rehearsal-is-not-scheduled-operation.md | see: 20260924T110141Z
Failure class: shared mutable receipt data corrupts checkpoint scope (R20).
Evidence: adding later run artifacts changed the first commit's recorded paths,
while exact Git inspection confirmed that the committed files remained correct.
Root cause: the run-wide artifact list and per-commit path list shared an object;
readback checked storage fidelity but not agreement with the represented commit.
Fix: reconstructed owned receipts from verified Git; the loop now requires
independent snapshots and exact-commit path comparison before checkpoint writes.
Verification: regression rejected the original aliasing and confirmed that
later artifact additions cannot change prior receipts; corrected readback matched.
No committed research was rolled back; no core governance or schedule changed.
Reflection: 20260924T110141Z.

## [ENT-006] | 2026-10-03 09:48 UTC | Neo | error | ref: agentic-brain:reflections/2026-10-03_neo_materiality-is-the-break-even-test-applied-to-attention.md | see: 20261003T094145Z
Failure class: a check or report spends attention it cannot justify (R20).
Evidence: the preflight GitHub check exited 1 while all three lookups succeeded,
because a trailing conditional set the final status. Several preflights repeated
that fixes were untested, which a failures-only log cannot show. The
supplier-finance check was first proposed without a materiality gate.
A scratch folder was also deleted with rm -rf on 2026-09-30, against the
recoverable-deletion rule.
Fix: preflight runs a check script whose exit status is the combined lookup
result, and treats no recurrence after a fix as normal. The framework check
starts with a materiality gate. workspace-ops names rm -rf inside combined
commands as the trap.
Verification: the script returned exit 0 with main for all three repositories.
Reflection: 20261003T094145Z.

## [ENT-007] | 2026-10-05 14:38 UTC | Neo | error | ref: agentic-brain:reflections/2026-10-05_neo_a-gate-passes-only-what-it-actually-reads.md | see: 20261005T143111Z
Scar: a gate failed open and committed one note past a failed evidence check.
Cause: the check's output was piped through grep and tail before the commit,
  so the pipeline returned tail's exit status, not the check's.
Related: a hand-resumed chain skipped a step; the rewritten gate then halted
  on a clean file because grep exits 1 when it finds nothing.
Fix: finish script redirects each check to a log and tests its own exit code,
  reruns whole after a stop; scan code 0 or output = hit, 1 = clean, >1 = error.
Gate: learnings-capture now forbids piped gates and requires a known-pass and
  known-fail test; rebuilt notes get an inbound-citation check before commit.
Reflection: 20261005T143111Z.

## [ENT-008] | 2026-10-07 08:05 UTC | Neo | error | ref: agentic-brain:reflections/2026-10-07_neo_a-sourced-sentence-fails-at-its-connectives-not-its-facts.md | see: 20261007T074552Z
Bug: fetch_text.py aborted a whole download batch when one URL failed
  (curl 92 on mckinsey.com; earlier an ASML release).
Fix: each URL is fetched independently; a failure prints FAILED, removes
  its partial file and the run exits 1 at the end; tested bad + good URL.
Scar: closure commit filter used git log --since with a UTC time, which
  git reads as local time, and pulled in pre-closure commits.
Gate: session-end skill pitfall: scope by <closure-commit>..HEAD.
Open: unsupported connective words beside sourced facts are caught only
  by reading; a gloss-check step is proposed, not built.
Reflection: 20261007T074552Z.
